.el .ds Aq '
.TH tapectl-report-needs 1  "tapectl-report-needs " 
.SH NAME
tapectl\-report\-needs \- Each unit\*(Aqs copy target, copies and shortfall at every location
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtapectl report needs\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-location\fR] [\fB\-\-all\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-\-home\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Each unit\*(Aqs copy target, copies and shortfall at every location
.PP
A unit\*(Aqs targets are its resolved `copies_at` map (an archive set\*(Aqs `required_locations` counts as one copy at each name), raised by the tape\-only multiplier for a tape\-only unit, and its copy floor is the larger of `min_copies` and the map\*(Aqs sum. Lists the units that have a target or are short of their copy floor; `\-\-all` lists every unit.
.PP
With `\-\-location`, only that location, and each unit\*(Aqs need there: group 1 when its target there is unmet, group 2 when it is short of its copy floor with no target there and no copy there yet.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Output in JSON format
.TP
\fB\-\-location\fR \fI<LOCATION>\fR
Only this location, with each unit\*(Aqs need there
.TP
\fB\-\-all\fR
Every unit, not only those with a target or a copy shortfall
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Show what would be done without making changes. Commands that cannot preview refuse the flag rather than ignore it
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Enable verbose output
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
No live progress on stderr. Long operations (stage create, volume write/resume/verify/read\-slices, restore) still write their session log under <home>/logs/
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip ADR\-0008 Tier\-2 confirmation prompts. It never reaches a Tier\-3 refusal — those are facts, not risks to accept
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fI<CONFIG>\fR
Path to config file.

NOTE: on its own this ALSO relocates the whole tapectl home to the config file\*(Aqs parent directory — database, keys, staging, stage reports. That is how every test harness gets an isolated home, so it still works, but it is surprising enough that it now warns. Use \-\-home when you mean "operate on a different archive", and \-\-config only to point at a config file inside that home.
.TP
\fB\-\-home\fR \fI<HOME>\fR
tapectl home directory: database, keys, catalogs, stage\-reports, logs.

Defaults to ~/.tapectl. The config file is taken from <home>/config.toml unless \-\-config overrides it. Also settable as TAPECTL_HOME.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
